365
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:07,800
You're a crooked doctor, or maybe you just know better.

366
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:12,280
So suppose that the surgery has a 90% chance of not killing.

367
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:13,640
10% chance of killing.

368
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:18,040
So 90% chance of surviving, 10% chance of dying.

369
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:27,240
90% chance you survive, 10% chance you'll die.

370
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:31,240
Now notice, if that's true, is that always true?

371
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:31,760
Yes.

372
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:34,120
Yes, these are two logically identical ways

373
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:37,720
of describing the very same distribution of events.

374
00:16:37,720 --> 00:16:40,200
Now, if anyone here ever worked in advertising or marketing

375
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:43,480
or anything, just common guess, just common sense,

376
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:45,600
which one do you want to use to sell someone

377
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:47,280
on your chart, your description, do you

378
00:16:47,280 --> 00:16:50,360
want to use to sell them on your surgery?

379
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:52,160
90% chance of surviving.

380
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:53,960
You've got a 90% chance of surviving.

381
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:56,340
Suppose you want to convince them to not get the surgery.

382
00:16:56,340 --> 00:16:59,080
Then you say, 10% chance of dying.

383
00:16:59,080 --> 00:17:01,320
You're going to die.

384
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:03,680
These are just two different ways

385
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:07,640
of organizing words to describe exactly the same events.

386
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:12,520
So if human beings had conscious preferences over outcomes,

